  "description": "GUHROS crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C82 H161 Ce4 Cr4 N9 O37,C2 H3 N1,H2 O1,6(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr3 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr4 (Cr) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.448-4.516 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.75-122.28°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C82H161Ce4Cr4N9O37·MeCN·H2O·6CH2Cl2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
